WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.601
-Last night was the big premiere
of "Tick, Tick... Boom!"

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:04.634
here in New York City.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:07.767
Man, I'm telling you,
oh, my gosh.

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:10.567
We all know how talented you
are, but you can do everything.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:14.334
-I mean, I don't know about
everything.

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:16.400
But, like, I grew up
doing musical theater.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.000
Like, that is my first passion,
that is my love and my joy,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.167
and nothing fills my heart more
than doing musical theater.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:26.434
And in the movie, I get to be,
like, Jonathan Larson's backup

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:29.300
vocalist in his one-man play,
"Tick, Tick... Boom!"

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.701
So the entire time, I'm
literally just up there, like,

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:36.901
jamming, grooving, supporting
my friend as Vanessa to Andrew,

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:39.667
but also, my character to
Jonathan, it's all very meta,

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:41.267
and it didn't even
feel like work.

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:43.801
-No, but let me tell you,
that scene with

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:46.234
you and Andrew Garfield,
that fast one

00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:48.100
where you're both
going and doing...

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.534
which must've taken, you know,
23 days just for that one scene.

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:54.634
It's amazing. It's
a showstopper. It is so good.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:58.567
-Thank you. It's choreographed
down to our eyeballs.

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:00.100
-It actually is.
-Actually.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.534
-You dance with your eyeballs.
-We danced with our eyeballs.

00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:06.334
-How did you come across
Lin-Manuel?

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:08.667
He was like, "Oh, we should talk
about a project,"

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:11.033
or did you know him before?
-Yeah, I had met him before.

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:13.634
My first time meeting him,
I went to see "Hamilton."

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:15.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
And it was right after --

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:17.300
Yes, of course. We love.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.133
And it was right after I did
"Grease Live!",

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:23.167
and so, Tommy Kail, my director,
his director,

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:24.267
there was like
a little connection.

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:26.634
I walk backstage
and I turn the corner,

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:30.334
and Lin's standing there with
his T-Birds, like, jacket --

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:32.300
leather jacket on, and I'm like,

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:36.067
"Oh, my God, you are
the coolest person ever."

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:39.000
-He's just so fun
and so creative and so positive.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.033
-And so kind.
-And kind too.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.801
-And supportive
and sees everyone.

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:46.033
-I feel like that would be
an amazing director.

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.901
-Yeah, the best director
because you feel safe.

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:52.234
Like, every day, he just, like,
shows up and has so much energy,

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:53.467
I don't know where
he gets it from,

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.434
because I'm sure he's not
getting a lot of sleep.

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:56.767
-He doesn't stop.

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.267
-He would come up to us,
tell us a note,

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:01.267
and be like, "Okay, good? Yeah."

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:02.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:04.534
And you're just like, "Oh, we're
doing steps now, okay."

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:05.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:06.834
-He would just do fun stuff
like that?

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:08.167
-He would do step routines
all the time,

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:09.534
left, right and center.

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:13.834
-And did you know much of
Jonathan Larson's story?

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:15.901
-I knew, like, a bit, yeah.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:20.067
Like, I obviously know
"Rent" intimately.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:23.000
I did it twice.
I played Maureen and Mimi.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.400
-Wow.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.234
-I love his work.
I love his community.

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:29.634
I love his stories, and, like,
he means so much to me

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:32.234
and my friends and my community,

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:35.701
of LGBTQ community
and of the theater.

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:40.133
And it's just, like, it feels
like none of this has been work

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:43.901
because we're talking about
something that is so dear to us.

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:46.901
And it's just like I feel like
I get to be a soldier of love

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:49.300
every day that I show up
talking about this movie.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.734
-Yeah, honestly,
when people see it --

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.334
[ Light clapping ]
Please sure.

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.300
I mean, it's amazing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.868
-It's so good.
-I think people will get that.

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:58.801
-Yeah.
-Because, you know, I think

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:01.234
you started maybe
coming on our show back --

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:02.868
It was "High School Musical,"
I want to say.

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:06.901
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:11.167
-And then "Princess Switch"
was on Netflix.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:13.133
That became the biggest thing
in the world.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:15.467
-Yeah, I have a new one
coming out this Thursday.

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:17.234
-You do?
-Yes, number three.

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:19.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
There's still three of me.

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:21.501
-I mean, come on.
-I know, it's crazy.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:24.567
-But I mean, I don't know,
I just love that you go like --

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:26.934
Usually, if you get one thing
that's a pop culture moment,

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:28.334
it's like, "That's great."
-I know.

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:31.901
-You got two massive ones,
and now, this thing I think is

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:34.300
a whole new career,
and just waking up and going,

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.567
"Oh, yeah, she knows
how to do this."

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:38.334
You know how to act,
and you know how to sing,

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:39.701
and when you see it,
it's moving.

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:41.133
The story is amazing.

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:44.000
If you love, just,
I think, like,

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.534
the American dream
and the struggle.

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:49.067
-Yeah. And also, like, it
focuses on a group of artists,

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:52.534
but the question that it asks is
universal, which is, "Am I

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:55.067
doing what I should be doing
with the time that I have?"

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:57.534
Because our time really is
so limited and, like,

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:59.968
it makes you be mindful
and really look at yourself

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:02.200
and be like,
"Okay, what are my priorities?"

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.167
And that's beautiful.
That's a gift.

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:05.133
-That's exactly right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.234
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:09.834
Here's Vanessa Hudgens
in "Tick, Tick... Boom!"

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:11.067
Take a look.

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:14.634
♪ -If I thought that
what you thought ♪

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:19.167
♪ Was that I hadn't thought
about sharing my thoughts ♪

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:25.667
♪ Then my reaction to
your reaction to my reaction ♪

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:29.667
♪ Would have been
more revealing ♪

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:31.400
-I have been rehearsing all day.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.367
I have been up since 4:00
this morning.

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:38.067
I've been trying to write a song
for a week and I am nowhere!

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:41.434
♪ I was afraid that you would be
afraid if I told you ♪

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:44.300
♪ That I was afraid
of intimacy ♪

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.334
-I've been telling you how
unhappy I am for months!

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:50.033
♪ -If you don't have a problem
with my problem ♪

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:53.601
♪ Maybe the problem's
simply co-dependency ♪

00:04:53.601 --> 00:04:56.000
Everyone's unhappy in New York!

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.901
That's what New York is!

00:04:57.901 --> 00:04:59.367
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:01.033
Vanessa Hudgens, everybody!

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:02.367
"Tick, Tick... Boom!"

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:04.801
is in theaters now
and on Netflix this Friday.

